            <ArticleTitle>Pisotriquetral loose body. An unusual cause of wrist pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>215-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A loose body flicking in and out of the pisotriquetral joint was found to be the cause of intermittent wrist pain and locking in two patients. Appropriate X-rays gave the diagnosis and surgical removal provided a satisfactory cure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
